      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Sociobiology and Controversy</strong><br>\nIn 1975, Wilson published \"Sociobiology: The New Synthesis,\" suggesting that social behavior has a genetic basis. This book sparked debate about the role of genetics in human behavior and society, with some critics arguing against its implications.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Pioneering Biodiversity</strong><br>\nWilson was a pioneer in the field of biodiversity. He stressed the importance of preserving natural habitats and species, warning about the consequences of human impact on the environment. His advocacy led to increased awareness and actions toward conservation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Honors and Awards</strong><br>\nWilson's work earned him many awards, including two Pulitzer Prizes for General Non-Fiction for \"On Human Nature\" and \"The Ants.\" He was also awarded the National Medal of Science for his contributions to understanding the living world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
