            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Writings and Influence</strong><br>\nWilson was a prolific writer, not just of scientific papers but also of books accessible to general audiences. His writing has influenced both scientific thought and public understanding of biology and ecology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>His Vision for the Future</strong><br>\nWilson was an advocate for the Half-Earth project, proposing that half of the Earth's land should be designated for biodiversity to preserve ecosystems. He believed this radical idea was essential to save our planet's species, including humans.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nEdward O. Wilson passed away on December 26, 2021, leaving behind a legacy as a champion of the natural world. His work continues to inspire biologists, conservationists, and nature lovers around the globe.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
